{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1761613,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Policy Shastra","festival_id":null,"organization_id":136795,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-25T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-11-04T15:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/policy-shastra-kamala-nehru-college-knc-du-delhi-1761613","region":"hybrid","details":"<p><strong>Ecophoria, The Economics Society of Kamala Nehru College, University of Delhi<\/strong> presents its case competition as the <strong>Policy Shastra<\/strong>, designed to challenge participants to approach complex real-world problems with analytical thinking, strategic insight and practical solutions.<\/p>\n<p>Participants will be challenged to look beyond policy design and examine how effective implementation can translate a well-designed policy into meaningful outcomes at the grassroots level with special focus on <strong>financial inclusion, access to formal credit, digital adoption and the economic empowerment of street vendors.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The competition brings together economic reasoning, data-driven analysis, strategic thinking and problem-solving, giving participants an opportunity to work through a realistic last-mile implementation challenge. Whether your interests lie in economics, consulting, finance, public policy, management or social entrepreneurship, this is your opportunity to test your ability to break down complex problems, develop actionable solutions and defend your ideas under pressure.<\/p>\n<h2><strong>Eligibility Criteria<\/strong><\/h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to <strong>undergraduate and postgraduate students<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Open to students from <strong>all courses, disciplines and academic years<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Team size: 2&ndash;4 members.<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Inter-college teams are permitted.<\/li>\n<li>Interdisciplinary teams are encouraged.<\/li>\n<li><strong>No prior policy experience is required.<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Deliverables:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Problem Diagnosis:<\/strong> Identify the key constraint and support the diagnosis using case data.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Stakeholder Strategy:<\/strong> Map vendors, ULBs, banks, BCs, fintechs, NGOs, vendor associations\/TVCs and other relevant stakeholders.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Outreach &amp; Awareness:<\/strong> Define target groups, communication channels, messaging and trust-building mechanisms.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Digital Adoption:<\/strong> Develop strategies to increase QR\/UPI adoption, digital literacy and transaction frequency.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Financial Plan:<\/strong> Provide a three-year projected cost, cost per vendor, funding sources and a cost-benefit rationale.<\/li>\n<li><strong>KPIs &amp; Monitoring:<\/strong> Define measurable indicators and a mechanism to track implementation.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Risk Management:<\/strong> Address defaults, digital fraud, low participation, administrative friction and funding constraints.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Scalability:<\/strong> Explain how a successful pilot can be expanded across multiple cities.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":4879033,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-09-25T18:52:27+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-03T00:30:57+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"rg8PD5p","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":46,"referral_leaderboard_show"